			"color":"#322",
			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n\n<Subject 1>: The same 25-year-old East Asian woman defined by <Picture 1>. Treat all four panels in <Picture 1> as different views of one person, not four people. Fully preserve her facial identity, warm natural skin, dark brown eyes, long dark hair styled half-up with braided sections, small pink floral hair ornaments, delicate hanging hair accessories, slim adult body proportions, and gentle natural smile. Fully preserve her complete outfit: a pale blush-pink traditional East Asian hanfu-inspired dress with a crossed collar, translucent long sleeves, layered flowing skirt, pink sash belt, embroidered pale-pink floral branches, and light embroidered cloth shoes.\n\n<Subject 2>: A bright open white-stone water courtyard and covered corridor with shallow reflective water, pale wooden columns, soft cream curtains, clean architectural lines, and abundant morning light. Use this as the new environment only. Do not reproduce the Character Sheet background or panel layout.\n\nsummary:\n\nreference generation\n\nretention_analysis:\n\nVisual:\n- <Picture 1>: fully_preserved for the woman's identity, hairstyle, hair ornaments, facial features, body proportions, garment construction, embroidery, sash, and shoes.\n- <Picture 1>: attribute_transfer for placing the same woman into the bright white-stone water courtyard.\n- <Picture 1>: weak_reference for the original white studio background and Character Sheet panel layout; do not reproduce either.\n\nAudio:\n- No Audio reference is provided. Generate a new natural courtyard soundscape and restrained non-diegetic music.\n\ndetailed_description:\n\nPhotorealistic live-action cinematic style in a bright, elegant white-stone water courtyard during a clear morning. Use <Subject 1> as the single visible woman and <Subject 2> as the environment. Preserve her identity, pink hanfu-inspired dress, embroidered floral details, half-up braided hairstyle, pink hair ornaments, and delicate accessories. The Character Sheet panels must never appear in the generated video. Only one instance of the woman may appear.\n\nThe video lasts exactly five seconds and uses one continuous stabilized shot.\n\n[Shot 1] Begin with a 40mm medium-wide frontal three-quarter view of <Subject 1> walking slowly along the covered corridor beside the shallow reflective water. Her full body, face, pale-pink dress, long sleeves, sash, hair ornaments, and embroidered shoes remain clearly visible. Morning light enters from the right and creates soft reflections on the water and translucent fabric.\n\n[0s-1.3s] She takes two small, natural steps toward the center of the corridor. Her skirt and translucent sleeves respond with restrained realistic movement. Her arms remain relaxed at her sides, and the embroidery stays fixed to the same garment panels.\n\n[1.3s-3.5s] She reaches a light cream curtain hanging at the end of the corridor and lifts it gently with her right hand. The curtain moves only from her contact and the mild morning air. She turns her upper body slightly toward the open courtyard, revealing her face in a soft three-quarter profile. Her long hair and hanging ornaments sway with small delayed motion and never change length, color, or structure.\n\n[3.5s-4.5s] She steps through the curtain and pauses beside the white-stone water edge. The camera performs one slow, low-amplitude lateral track of approximately 60 degrees from her frontal three-quarter view toward her right profile, maintaining a similar distance and height. The water, columns, curtain, dress, face, and hair remain spatially consistent.\n\n[4.5s-5s] She releases the curtain, turns her gaze toward the bright courtyard, and holds a calm, gentle expression. The curtain settles naturally behind her. Hold the final composition for the last half-second with her face, complete outfit, hair ornaments, reflective water, and white architecture clearly readable.\n\nCamera and transitions: one continuous stabilized shot with one slow lateral track. No cuts, dissolves, zoom jumps, handheld shake, sudden focus changes, duplicated body parts, identity changes, outfit changes, or impossible movement.\n\nConstraints: exactly one woman, one corridor, one cream curtain, one water courtyard, and one continuous pink outfit. No Character Sheet panels, four-panel layout, duplicated woman, second face, extra limbs, extra fingers, missing hair ornaments, changed hairstyle, changed embroidery, transparent body, floating fabric, fantasy glow, subtitles, logos, watermarks, or readable text.\n\noverall_soundscape:\n\nQuiet open courtyard ambience continues throughout. Soft water movement, faint morning birds, restrained footsteps on pale stone, and gentle fabric friction remain spatially natural. The curtain produces one light cloth sound when her hand lifts it and settles with a soft rustle after she releases it. No dialogue, speech, or unrelated sound effects.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\n\nSoft restrained music uses sparse guqin-like plucked strings, warm bamboo flute, and a very light sustained pad at a slow tempo. The music remains beneath the courtyard ambience, becomes slightly fuller as she steps into the open courtyard, and resolves with one delicate warm chord during the final half-second hold."
